$DATUM A mixture of this material (0.19 g, 1 mmol), tert-butyl
piperazine-1-carboxylate (0.19 g, 1 mmol), sodium triacetoxyborohydride
(0.23 g, 1.1 mmol) and 1,2-dichloroethane (5 mL) was stirred at at 20°C
for 3 h then was allowed to stand for 64 h. Resulting mixture was
partitioned between saturated aqueous NaHCO3 (30 mL) and CH2Cl2 (2 x 20
mL). Combined organic extracts were dried (Na2SO4) and evaporated in
vacuo to give an oil. Chromatography (SiO2, 0-50% EtOAc in petrol). The
title compound (0.30 g, 83%) as a colorless oil. tert-Butyl
4-{[2-methoxy-4-(prop-2-yn-1-yloxy)phenyl]methyl}piperazine-1-carboxylate
(17). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): 7.24 (1H, d), 6.63-6.48 (2H, m), 4.70 (2H,
d), 3.81 (3H, s), 3.53 (2H, s), 3.50-3.24 (4H, m), 2.55 (1H, t),
2.51-2.17 (4H, m), 1.47 (9H, s). MS, m/z 361 [M+H]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Structure-Based Design of Type II Inhibitors Applied to Maternal
Embryonic Leucine Zipper Kinase
