$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of 3(R)-1-benzyl-3-phenyl-4-(trifluoroacetyl)piperazin-2-one
(6p). To a 0 °C stirring suspension of D-phenylglycine methyl ester
hydrochloride (100 mg, 0.496 mmol, 1.0 equiv.), 4Å powdered molecular
sieves (200 mg), acetic acid (84 μL, 1.5 mmol, 3.0 equiv.) and sodium
triacetoxyborohydride (158 mg, 0.744 mmol, 1.5 equiv.) in 5 mL
acetonitrile was added dropwise over 5 minutes a 2.5 mL acetonitrile
solution of aldehyde 4f (134 mg, 0.546 mmol, 1.1 equiv.). After stirring
for 90 minutes, the ice bath was removed and the reaction was warmed to
ambient temperature and stirred for 40 hours. The mixture was poured into
aqueous saturated NaHCO3, which was extracted three times with
dichloromethane. The combined organic extracts were dried (Na2SO4),
filtered and concentrated in vacuo. Purification by flash chromatography
(0 to 30% EtOAc in hexanes) provided piperazinone 6p (145 mg, 81%). HRMS
(ES) exact mass calcd for C19H18F3N2O2 (M+H+): 363.1315; found 363.1310.
Chiral HPLC analysis (Chiralcel OD column 250 X 4.6 mm; 220 nm; flow =
1.0 mL/minute of A/B:9/1 (A = 0.1% diethylamine in hexanes, B = ethanol);
20 minute run. 95.4% enantiomeric excess. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3)
(Rotamer A:B; 3.5:1) Rotamer A: δ 7.44-7.26 (m, 9H), 7.25-7.20 (m, 1H),
6.27 (s, 1H), 4.99 (d, J = 14.6 Hz, 1H), 4.45 (d, J = 14.4 Hz, 1H), 3.91
(br d, J = 14.2 Hz, 1H), 3.61 (td, J = 12.6, 3.8 Hz, 1H), 3.46 (td, J =
11.7, 4.6 Hz, 1H), 3.30 (dt, J = 12.4, 3.0 Hz, 1H): Rotamer B: δ
7.44-7.26 (m, 9H), 7.25- 7.20 (m, 1H), 5.82 (s, 1H), 4.84 (d, J = 14.6
Hz, 1H), 4.50 (d, J = 14.6 Hz, 1H), 4.26-4.17 (m, 1H), 3.44-3.34 (m, 2H),
3.21-3.14 (m, 1H).Retention time for 6p = 8.2 minutes (Area % = 91.85),
enantiomer retention time = 10.7 minutes (Area % = 2.14);
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM mol. sieves used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Preparation of Substituted Piperazinones via Tandem Reductive
Amination-(N,N'-Acyl Transfer)-Cyclization
