$DATUM Preparation of Benzyl 2(R)-2,4-dibenzyl-3-oxopiperazine-1-carboxylate
(6f). To a 0 °C stirring suspension of D-phenylalanine methyl ester
hydrochloride (100 mg, 0.464 mmol, 1.0 equiv.), 4Å powdered molecular
sieves (200 mg), acetic acid (80 μL, 1.39 mmol, 3.0 equiv.) and sodium
triacetoxyborohydride (148 mg, 0.696 mmol, 1.5 equiv.) in 5 mL
acetonitrile was added dropwise over 5 minutes a 2.5 mL acetonitrile
solution of aldehyde 4g (145 mg, 0.510 mmol, 1.1 equiv.). After stirring
for 90 minutes, the ice bath was removed and the reaction was warmed to
ambient temperature and stirred for 18 hours. The pressure tube was
sealed and heated to 120 °C for 72 hours, cooled and poured into aqueous
saturated NaHCO3, which was extracted three times with dichloromethane.
The combined organic extracts were dried (Na2SO4), filtered and
concentrated in vacuo. Purification by flash chromatography (0 to 50%
ethyl acetate in dichloromethane) provided piperazinone 6g as clear oil
(156 mg, 81% yield). Chiral HPLC analysis (Chiralcel OD column 250 X 4.6
mm; 220 nm; flow = 1.0 mL/minute of A/B:90/10 (A=hexanes, B=ethanol); 45
minute run. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.38-7.10 (m, 15H), 5.06 (br d, J =
12.2 Hz, 1H), 4.94 (br d, J = 13.9 Hz, 1H), 4.80-4.5 (m, 1H), 4.23(br d,
J = 14.6 Hz, 1H), 4.02 (br d, J = 12.7 Hz, 1H), 3.50-3.20 (m, 3H), 2.88
(br d, J = 11.0 Hz, 1H), 2.80-2.50 (m, 2H) . HRMS (ES) exact mass
calculated for C26H27N2O3 (M+H+): 415.2016; found 415.2014. Retention
time for 6g = 33.9 minutes (Area % = 57.9), enantiomer retention time =
29.6 minutes (Area % = 22.53); 44.0% enantiomeric excess.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM mol. sieves used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Preparation of Substituted Piperazinones via Tandem Reductive
Amination-(N,N'-Acyl Transfer)-Cyclization
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Beshore, Douglas C.; Dinsmore, Christopher J.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2002), 4(7), 1201-1204

