$DATUM 5-(Benzyloxymethyl)-7-({[(4S)-2,2-dimethyl-1,3-dioxolan-4-yl](2-
hydroxyethyl)amino}methyl)-4-methoxy-5H-pyrrolo[3,2-d]pyrimidine
(90).(S)-2-[(2,2- Dimethyl-1,3-dioxolan-4-yl)methylamino]ethanol (48 mg,
0.27 mmol), MgSO4 (500 mg), aldehyde 448 (81 mg, 0.27 mmol), and sodium
triacetoxyborohydride (75 mg, 0.36 mmol) were stirred together at room
temperature in 1,2-dichloroethane (3 mL) for 16 h. The mixture was then
diluted with CH2Cl2 and washed with saturated aqueous NaHCO3 solution,
dried, filtered, and the filtrate concentrated in vacuo. The resulting
residue was purified by chromatography (EtOAc→ EtOAc/MeOH/28% aq NH4OH =
97: 3:0.01) to afford 90 (100 mg, 80%) as a colorless gum, which turned
pale-yellow on standing. 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 8.53 (s, 1H), 7.36-7.23 (s,
6H), 5.71 (s, 2H), 4.60 (br s, exchanged to D2O, 1H), 4.46 (s, 2H), 4.20
(pentet, J = 6.3 Hz, 1H), 4.10 (s, 3H), 4.02 (d, J = 14.1 Hz, 1H),
3.88-3.67 (m, 4H), 3.26 (dd, J = 8.0, 6.9 Hz, 1H), 2.86-2.70 (m, 3H),
2.61 (dd, J = 13.2, 6.7 Hz, 1H), 1.32 (s, 3H), 1.28 (s, 3H). 13C NMR
(CDCl3, center line at δ 77.0): δ 156.3, 150.2, 149.9, 136.8, 131.5,
128.5, 128.0, 127.7, 116.2, 115.1, 108.9, 76.9, 74.2, 70.1, 68.4, 59.9,
57.2, 56.5, 53.6, 47.8, 26.8, 25.4. ESI-HRMS for C24H33N4O5 [MH+] calcd,
457.2451; found, 457.2469.
