$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure A. Reductive alkylation
step: To a RB-flask equipped with magnetic stir-bar and temperature probe
was charged the arylamine (100 mol%) and the carbonyl compound (110 mol%)
followed by i-PrOAc (12 mL/g of arylamine) and trifluoroacetic acid (200
mol%). Sodium triacetoxyborohydride (120 mol%) was added as a solid over
1 min, normally accompanied by an increase in temperature to ~ 40 °C.
After 10 min agitation, the mixture was usually homogeneous and LC
analysis indicated complete consumption of the arylamine. A solution of
10 wt% aqueous NaOH was added to the mixture until pH 8-9. The phases
were allowed to separate and the organic phase washed with brine then
dried over Na2SO4, filtered and concentrated to afford the crude
product.1Urea formation step: To a RB-flask equipped with a magnetic
stir-bar and temperature probe was charged with THF (< 50 ppm H2O, 8
mL/mL of CSI) then chlorosulfonyl isocyanate (CSI) (120 mol%) was added
at room temperature. The mixture was cooled to -10 °C. A solution of
reductively alkylated amine (100 mol%) in THF : i-PrOAc (1 : 1) (< 500
ppm H2O, 5 mL/g of amine) and added over a 20 min period. An exotherm was
observed during this addition (max. temp. 2 °C). After 10 min and with
the batch temperature returned to -10 °C, water (0.5 mL/g of substrate)
was added dropwise over a 10 min period. A second exotherm was observed
during the water addition (max. temp. 17 °C). The mixture was allowed to
warm to rt and aged for 30 min. The mixture was treated with 10% aq. NaOH
until pH 8-9 and the separated organic phase was washed with brine. The
work-up was conducted at 50 °C to maintain solubility of the product.
Azeotropic drying with i-PrOAc was conducted at atmospheric pressure
under constant volume conditions until the water content was < 250 ppm by
KF titration (THF was also removed during this process). The urea was
isolated by crystallization. 1-Benzyl-1-(2-chloro-4-methyl-phenyl)urea
(3l): Following general procedure A, 3l was obtained as an off-white
solid (80%) 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO) δ 2.26 (s, 3H), 3.88-4.38 (br, 1H),
4.96-5.38 (br, 1H), 5.69 (br s, 2H), 6.86 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 7.01 (d, J
= 8.0 Hz, 1H), 7.12-7.29 (m, 5H), 7.34 (s, 1H); 13C {1H} NMR (100 MHz,
DMSO) δ 20.7, 51.6, 127.3, 128.5, 128.6, 129.0, 131.0, 131.5, 132.7,
136.6, 138.8, 139.4, 157.6. HRMS calcd. for C15H15ClN2O [M+H]+ 275.09457,
found 275.09479.
