$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of Benzyl 3(S)-4-acetyl-1-benzyl-3-methylpiperazin-2-one
(6i). To a 0 °C stirring suspension of L-alanine methyl ester
hydrochloride (60 mg, 0.430 mmol, 1.0 equiv.), 4Å powdered molecular
sieves (200 mg), acetic acid (74 μL, 1.29 mmol, 3.0 equiv.) and sodium
triacetoxyborohydride (136 mg, 0.645 mmol, 1.5 equiv.) in 5 mL
acetonitrile was added dropwise over 5 minutes a 2.5 mL acetonitrile
solution of aldehyde 4a (99 mg, 0.52 mmol, 1.2 equiv.). After stirring
for 90 minutes, the ice bath was removed and the reaction was warmed to
ambient temperature and stirred for 18 hours. The reaction was heated to
reflux for 3 hours, cooled and poured into aqueous saturated NaHCO3,
which was extracted three times with dichloromethane. The combined
organic extracts were dried (Na2SO4), filtered and concentrated in vacuo.
Purification by flash chromatography (0 to 50% ethyl acetate in
dichloromethane) provided piperazinone 6i as clear oil (85 mg, 80%
yield). Chiral HPLC analysis (Chiralcel OD column 250 X 4.6 mm; 220 nm;
flow = 1.0 mL/minute of A/B:90/10 (A=hexanes, B=ethanol); 25 minute
run.99.0% enantiomeric excess. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) (Rotamer A:B; 2:1)
Rotamer A: δ 7.37-7.28 (m, 3H), 7.26-7.21 (m, 2H), 4.82 (d, J = 14.4 Hz,
1H), 4.62-4.52 (m, 1H), 4.46 (q, J = 7.1 Hz, 1H), 4.38 (d, J = 14.6 Hz,
1H), 3.40-3.26 (m, 1H), 3.22-3.12 (m, 1H), 3.01 (td, J = 12.0, 3.9 Hz,
1H), 2.13 (s, 3H), 1.57 (d, J = 7.1 Hz, 3H); Rotamer B: δ 7.37-7.28 (m,
3H), 7.26-7.21 (m, 2H), 5.10 (q, J = 7.0 Hz, 1H),4.68 (d, J = 14.6 Hz,
1H), 4.62-4.52 (m, 1H), 3.76-3.68 (m, 1H), 3.50 (td, J = 11.0, 3.5 Hz,
