$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Experimental for Solid Phase Synthesis of indinavir: 250 mg of Rapp
TentaGel S COOH resin (0.25mmol/g) was added to a reaction vessel and
suspended in 5 ml CH2Cl2/DMF (4:1). The slurry was treated with 2 (5 eq),
EDC (5 eq) and DMAP (2 eq) overnight then filtered and washed three times
each with DMF, 2-propanol and CH2Cl2. To the resin 3 was added 5 ml 30%
TFA/CH2Cl2 and the slurry mixed for 1 h then filtered and washed three
times each with CH2Cl2, 10% Et3N/ CH2Cl2, CH2Cl2. To the resulting resin
in 5 ml CH2Cl2/DMF (4:1) was added 4 (2.5 eq), EDC (5 eq), HOBt (5 eq)
and Et3N (6 eq). After mixing overnight, the resin was filtered and
washed three times each with DMF, 2-propanol and CH2Cl2. Resin 5 was
suspended in CH2Cl2 (4 ml) and TFA (2 ml) was added. The mixture was
agitated for 0.5 h and then filtered and washed three times each with
CH2Cl2, 10% Et3N/ CH2Cl2, CH2Cl2, DMF. The resulting resin in 4 ml 1%
AcOH/DMF was treated with 6 (10 eq) and NaB(OAc)3H (10 eq) overnight.
Then the resin was filtered and washed three times each with DMF,
2-propanol and CH2Cl2. Resin 7 in 5 ml THF was added HF/pyridine (0.5 ml)
was mixed at rt for 6 h. Then the resin was filtered and washed three
times each with THF, DMF, 2-propanol and CH2Cl2. The cleavage was
performed with 3 ml of 9:1 MeOH/Et3N at 50 °C overnight The resin was
removed by filtration and the sample was concentrated to dryness. Table
1, Entry b, Indinavir, yield 80% HPLC Purity: >95%
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, RESIN SUPPORTED REACTION
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Solid Phase Synthesis of Indinavir and Its Analogues
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
