$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of N-p-chlorophenylmethyl rotaxane 2g: (Table 2, entry 12) In a
screw cap tube a suspension of rotaxane 1 (49 mg, 50 μmol),
p-chlorobenzaldehyde (0.15 g, 1.0 mmol), sodium
tri(benzoyloxy)borohydride 5f (0.16 g, 0.75 mmol), and triethylamine
(0.14 mL, 1.0 mmol) in dry NMP (0.5 mL) was heated to 70 °C for 16 h.
After cooling to r.t., 5 mL of water was added to the mixture and the
aqueous mixture was extracted three times with chloroform (10 mL). The
combined organic layer was dried over MgSO4 and concentrated under
reduced pressure. The residue was purified by short column chromatography
(aluminium oxide, EtOAc) and recrystallized from chloroform /2-propanol
to give 2g (79% conversion, isolated: 25 mg, 27 μmol, 54%) as a colorless
solid. m.p. 165.1-166.1 °C; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3, 298 K) δ 8.21 (d, J =
8.0 Hz, 2H), 8.10 (s, 2H), 7.24 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 2H),7.18 (d, J = 8.3 Hz,
2H), 7.15 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 2H), 7.07 (s, 1H), 6.92-6.82 (m, 11H), 5.98 (s,
2H), 4.10-4.02 (m, 8H), 3.69-3.61 (m, 8H), 3.37 (s, 6H), 3.20-3.17 (m,
4H), 2.83-2.80 (m, 4H), 2.27 (s, 6H), 2.18 (s, 6H) ppm; 13C NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3, 298 K) δ 167.0, 148.5, 139.4, 138.6, 137.6, 137.4, 136.4, 136.3,
134.0, 132.1, 130.0, 128.7, 128.4, 128.1, 127.9, 126.6, 120.4, 111.4,
69.4, 69.1, 67.9, 66.8, 57.7, 57.6, 56.6, 21.3, 20.7 ppm; IR (KBr) ν 2920
(νC-H, as), 2875 (νC-H, as), 1709 (νC=O as), 1505 (νC=C, as), 1217
(νC(=O)-O-C, as), 1053 (νC-O-C, as) cm-1; FAB-HR-MS calcd for
C57H67ClNO10 [M+ H]+ 960.4454, found 960.4464.
