$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of
3(R)-1-benzyl-3-iso-propyl-4-(trifluoroacetyl)piperazin-2-one (6o). To a
0 °C stirring suspension of D-valine methyl ester hydrochloride (100 mg,
0.597 mmol, 1.0 equiv.), 4Å powdered molecular sieves (200 mg), acetic
acid (102 μL, 1.79 mmol, 3.0 equiv.) and sodium triacetoxyborohydride
(190 mg, 0.895 mmol, 1.5 equiv.) in 5 mL acetonitrile was added dropwise
over 5 minutes a 2.5 mL acetonitrile solution of aldehyde 4f (161 mg,
0.657 mmol, 1.1 equiv.). After stirring for 90 minutes, the ice bath was
removed and the reaction was warmed to ambient temperature and stirred
for 40 hours. The mixture was poured into aqueous saturated NaHCO3, which
was extracted three times with dichloromethane. The combined organic
extracts were dried (Na2SO4), filtered and concentrated in vacuo.
Purification by flash chromatography (0 to 30% ethyl acetate in hexanes)
provided piperazinone 6o (155 mg, 79%). Chiral HPLC analysis (Chiralcel
OD column 250 X 4.6 mm; 220 nm; flow = 1.0 mL/minute of A/B:9/1 (A = 0.1%
diethylamine in hexanes, B = ethanol); 20 minute run. >99% enantiomeric
excess. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.40-7.28 (m, 4H), 7.27-7.20 (m, 1H),
4.95 (d, J = 14.6 Hz, 1H), 4.89 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 1H), 4.31 (d, J = 14.6
Hz, 1H), 3.98 (br d, J = 14.4 Hz, 1H), 3.61 (ddd, J = 15.1, 11.6, 4.0 Hz,
1H), 3.38 (td, J = 12.1, 4.4 Hz, 1H), 3.23 (ddd, J = 12.3, 4.1, 2.1 Hz,
1H). HRMS (ES) exact mass calcd for C16H20F3N2O2 (M+H+): 329.1471; found
329.1455.Retention time for 6o = 6.9 minutes (Area % = 87.02), enantiomer
retention time = 8.9 minutes (Area % = 0);
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM mol. sieves used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Preparation of Substituted Piperazinones via Tandem Reductive
Amination-(N,N'-Acyl Transfer)-Cyclization
