$DATUM (3S,4R,5S,6R,7R)-3,4,5,6,7-Pentakis(benzyloxy)-1-butylazocane (21a). To a
solution of 20 (204 mg, 0.317 mmol) and butyraldehyde (27 μL, 0.30 mmol)
in 1,2-dichloroethane (1.5 mL) at room temperature was added NaBH(OAc)3
(94 mg, 0.44 mmol). The reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature
for 16 h, diluted with EtOAc (30 mL), and washed with saturated NaHCO3 (2
× 10 mL). The organic layer was dried over anhydrous MgSO4 and
concentrated under reduced pressure. The crude product was purified by
silica column chromatography (first purification EtOAc/hexanes 1:1,
second purification MeOH/CH2Cl2 1:18). 21a as a yellowish oil (175 mg,
79%). [α]26 D +20.2 (c 1.00 CHCl3); IR (neat) 3063, 3030, 2930, 2862,
1679, 1496, 1454, 1360, 1206, 1072, 735, 698 cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 7.43-7.20 (m, 25H), 4.94 (d, J = 10.3 Hz, 1H), 4.88 (d, J = 12.1
Hz, 1H), 4.81 (d, J = 12.1 Hz, 1H), 4.79 (d, J = 12.1 Hz, 1H), 4.74 (d, J
= 10.3 Hz, 1H), 4.70 (d, J = 11.6 Hz, 1H), 4.57 (d, J = 11.6 Hz, 1H),
4.49 (d, J = 12.1 Hz, 1H), 4.30 (d, J = 12.1 Hz, 1H), 4.22 (s, 1H), 4.19
(d, J = 12.1 Hz, 1H), 4.09 (t, J = 8.8 Hz, 1H), 3.88 (d, J = 9.4 Hz, 1H),
3.33 (ddd, J = 10.6, 8.0, 2.8 Hz, 1H), 3.12-3.01 (m, 2H), 2.79 (dd, J =
13.2, 10.8 Hz, 1H), 2.64 (dd, J = 14.7, 3.2 Hz, 1H), 2.59 (dd, J = 13.6,
5.7 Hz, 1H), 2.42 (m, 1H), 2.25 (m, 1H), 1.17 (br m, 4H), 0.83 (t, J =
7.0 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 139.4, 139.1, 138.9, 138.6,
128.4, 128.3, 128.2, 128.1, 128.0, 127.9, 127.5, 127.4, 127.3, 84.0,
83.4, 82.3, 81.9, 76.4, 74.2, 74.0, 73.1, 71.1, 57.8, 57.7, 55.1, 30.5,
20.4, 14.1; HRMS (ESI) calcd for [C46H53NO5 + H]+ 700.3996, found
700.4004.
