$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of 3(R)-1,3-dibenzyl-4-iso-butyrylpiperazin-2-one (6c). To a
0 °C stirring suspension of D-phenylalanine methyl ester hydrochloride
(100 mg, 0.464 mmol, 1.0 equiv.), 4Å powdered molecular sieves (200 mg),
acetic acid (80 μL, 1.4 mmol, 3.0 equiv.) and sodium
triacetoxyborohydride (148 mg, 0.696 mmol, 1.5 equiv.) in 5 mL
acetonitrile was added a 2.5 mL acetonitrile solution of aldehyde 4c (112
mg, 0.510 mmol, 1.1 equiv.) dropwise. After stirring for 90 minutes, the
ice bath was removed and the reaction was warmed to ambient temperature
and stirred for 18 hours. The pressure tube was sealed and heated to 120
°C for 4 days, cooled and poured into aqueous saturated NaHCO3, which was
extracted three times with dichloromethane. The combined organic extracts
were dried (Na2SO4), filtered and concentrated in vacuo. Purification by
flash chromatography (0 to 60% ethyl acetate in hexanes) provided
piperazinone 6c as clear oil (126 mg, 78% yield). Chiral HPLC analysis
(Chiralcel OD column 250 X 4.6 mm; 220 nm; flow = 1.0 mL/minute of
A/B:90/10 (A=0.1% diethylamine in hexanes, B=ethanol); 30 minute run.
15.2% enantiomeric excess. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) (Rotamer A:B; 3:2
Rotamer A: δ 7.36-7.27 (m, 4H), 7.25-7.06 (m, 6H), 4.92 (d, J = 14.6 Hz,
1H), 4.62 (dd, J = 10.0, 3.2 Hz, 1H), 4.35 (d, J = 14.6 Hz, 1H), 3.37
(dd, J = 13.7, 3.4 Hz, 1H), 3.34-3.26 (m, 1H), 3.24- 3.10 (m, 2H), 3.06
(dd, J = 12.1, 4.0 Hz, 1H), 2.90 (td, J = 13.4, 3.9 Hz, 1H), 2.63 (sept,
J = 6.8 Hz, 1H), 0.92 (d, J = 7.1 Hz, 3H), 0.60 (d, J = 6.6 Hz, 3H):
Rotamer B: δ 7.36-7.27 (m, 4H), 7.25-7.06 (m, 6H), 5.27 (t, J = 5.0 Hz,
1H), 4.93 (d, J = 14.9 Hz, 1H), 4.66 (dd, J = 13.7, 4.4 Hz, 1H), 4.30 (d,
J = 14.6 Hz, 1H), 3.56-3.50 (m, 1H), 3.49 (dd, J = 13.5, 4.2 Hz, 1H),
3.34-3.26 (m, 1H), 2.82 (dt, J = 12.2, 2.9 Hz, 1H), 2.58 (qd, J = 11.5,
3.0 Hz, 1H), 2.05 (m, 1H), 1.09 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 1.08 (d, J = 7.1 Hz,
1H). HRMS (ES) exact mass calculated for C22H27N2O2 (M+H+): 351.2067;
found 351.2085.Retention time for 6c = 10.7 minutes (Area % = 47.98),
enantiomer retention time = 18.9 minutes (Area % = 35.32);
