$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Reductive Amination To a mixture of 2-aminoacetanilide (7 g, 46.6 mmol),
ketone (51.3 mmol, 1.1 eq.), and NaBH(OAc)3 (14.8 g, 70 mmol. 1.5 eq.) in
CH2Cl2 (56 mL) at 0-5 °C, was added AcOH (10.6 mL, 6.0 eq.), maintaining
the internal temperature at <= 20°C. The solution was stirred at
approximately 20°C for 4 h or until complete by HPLC. MTHF (140 mL), was
added to the mixture and the pH was adjusted to 13 with 10 N NaOH (50
mL). Where required, the biphasic mixture was heated to maintain a
solution. The organic layer was washed with H2O (70 mL) and reduced under
vacuum by approximately 60%. Heptane was added as an anti solvent, and
the resulting solid was isolated via filtration and dried under vacuum at
approximately 50 °C. Where required, the compound was recrystallized or
purified chromatographically to provide an analytically pure sample.
Yields: 55-90%.
N-(2-{[1-(Phenylmethyl)-4-piperidinyl]amino}phenyl)acetamide (1b), yield
77%. 1H NMR (DMSO-d6): δ 9.09 (s, 1H), 7.28-7.33 (m, 4H), 7.22-7.25 (m,
1H), 7.12 (d, J = 7.6 Hz, 1H), 6.97 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 6.65 (d, J = 8.0
Hz, 1H), 6.53 (t, J = 7.6 Hz, 1H), 4.59 (d, J = 7.6 Hz, 1H), 3.46 (s,
2H), 3.22-3.29 (m, 1H), 2.76 (d, J = 11.6 Hz, 2H), 2.08 (t, J = 11.2 Hz,
2H), 2.03 (s, 3H), 1.9 (d, J = 11.2 Hz, 2H), 1.41 (q, J = 11.6 Hz, 2 H).
13C NMR (DMSO-d6): δ 168.5, 141.2, 138.7, 128.7, 128.1, 126.8, 126.1,
126.0, 123.8, 115.5, 111.6,62.2,51.9,49.1,31.8,23.4. Mp: 159.0-160.3 °C.
HRMS: calc. for C20H26N3O: 324.2076. Found 324.2076.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM General Synthesis of 1-Substituted 2-Methylbenzimidazoles from Ketones
and 2-Aminoacetanilide
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Burova, Svetlana A.; Davis, Roman; Fitzgerald, Russ N.; Johnson, Byron
S.; Matsuoka, Richard T.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2007), 37(18), 3029-3039

