$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of Benzyl 3(S)-4-acetyl-1-benzyl-3-iso-butylpiperazin-2-one
(6j). To a 0 °C stirring suspension of L-leucine methyl ester
hydrochloride (153 mg, 0.842 mmol, 1.0 equiv.), 4Å powdered molecular
sieves (200 mg), acetic acid (140 μL, 2.53 mmol, 3.0 equiv.) and sodium
triacetoxyborohydride (268 mg, 1.26 mmol, 1.5 equiv.) in 5 mL
acetonitrile was added dropwise over 5 minutes a 2.5 mL acetonitrile
solution of aldehyde 4a (177 mg, 0.930 mmol, 1.1 equiv.). After stirring
for 90 minutes, the ice bath was removed and the reaction was warmed to
ambient temperature and stirred for 18 hours. The reaction was heated to
reflux for 10 hours, cooled and poured into aqueous saturated NaHCO3,
which was extracted three times with dichloromethane. The combined
organic extracts were dried (Na2SO4), filtered and concentrated in vacuo.
Purification by flash chromatography (5% methanol in dichloromethane)
provided piperazinone 6j as a white solid (186 mg, 77% yield). Chiral
HPLC analysis (Chiralcel AD column 250 X 4.6 mm; 220 nm; flow = 1.0
mL/minute of A/B:85/15 (A=hexanes, B=2-propanol); 20 minute run. 92%
enantiomeric excess. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) (Rotamer A:B; 1.2:1) Rotamer
A: δ 7.37-7.33 (m, 2H), 7.32-7.28 (m, 1H), 7.25-7.21 (m, 2H), 4.84 (d, J
= 14.6 Hz, 1H), 4.37 (dd, J = 8.1, 6.1 Hz, 1H), 4.31 (d, J = 14.4 Hz,
1H), 3.74-3.69 (m, 1H), 3.38-3.30 (m, 1H), 3.18- 3.03 (m, 2H), 2.13 (s,
3H), 1.94-1.88 (m, 1H), 1.73-1.60 (m, 2H), 1.03 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 3H), 1.02
(d, J = 8.3 Hz, 3H); Rotamer B: δ 7.37-7.33 (m, 2H), 7.32-7.28 (m, 1H),
7.25-7.21 (m, 2H), 5.24 (dd, J = 9.5, 4.4 Hz, 1H), 4.72 (d, J = 14.6 Hz,
1H), 4.58-4.51(m, 1H), 4.47 (d, J = 14.6 Hz, 1H), 3.52 (ddd, J = 15.1,
11.5, 4.0 Hz, 1H), 3.38-3.30 (m, 1H), 3.18-3.03 (m, 1H), 2.11 (s, 3H),
1.87-1.75 (m, 2H), 1.73-1.60 (m, 1H), 1.04 (d, J = 4.6 Hz, 3H), 0.96 (d,
J = 6.6 Hz, 3H). HRMS (ES) exact mass calculated for C17H25N2O2 (M+H+):
289.1912; found 289.1915.Retention time for 6j = 8.5 minutes (Area % =
81.4), enantiomer retention time = 13.2 minutes (Area % = 3.5);
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM mol. sieves used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Preparation of Substituted Piperazinones via Tandem Reductive
Amination-(N,N'-Acyl Transfer)-Cyclization
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Beshore, Douglas C.; Dinsmore, Christopher J.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2002), 4(7), 1201-1204

