$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Method B. Reductive Amination Using
NaBH(OAc)3. NaBH(OAc)3 (1-1.5 equiv) was added in portions to a solution
of an aldehyde or ketone and a primary or secondary amine in
dichloroethane (DCE) or THF. In some cases, 1 equiv of HOAc was added to
the mixture before the addition of NaBH(OAc)3. After the reaction was
complete, the mixture was diluted with sat. NaHCO3 and extracted with
EtOAc or CH2Cl2, and the extracts were washed with brine. The organic
solution was dried and evaporated and the residue purified by
chromatography, trituration or crystallization.
(2E)-N-Hydroxy-3-[4-[[4-(1H-indol-3-yl)-1-piperidinyl]-methyl]phenyl]-2-propenamide
14j. Following Method B, 3-(piperidin-4-yl)-1H-indole (2.00 g, 10 mmol),
10 (1.90 g, 10 mmol), and NaBH(OAc)3 (1 equiv) were reacted in DCE to
afford
(2E)-3-[4-[4-(1H-indol-3-yl)piperidin-1-ylmethyl]phenyl]-2-propenoic acid
methyl ester (2.90 g, 77%). 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 1.90 (m, 2H), 2.07 (m, 3H),
2.24 (t, 11.1 Hz, 2H), 2.88 (m, 1H), 3.06 (d, 11.3 Hz, 2H), 3.64 (s, 2H),
3.84 (s, 3H), 6.47 (d, 16.2 Hz, 1H), 7.00 (d, 1.9 Hz, 1H), 7.13 (m, 1H),
7.21 (m, 1H), 7.40 (m, 3H), 7.54 (m, 2H), 7.71 (m, 2H), 8.06 (s, 1H); 13C
NMR (CDCl3) δ 33.36, 33.83, 52.15, 54.81, 63.57, 111.63, 117.78, 119.52,
120.09, 122.35, 127.09, 128.48, 130.18, 133.67, 136.79, 145.16, 167.99;
m/z 375 (MH+).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM N-Hydroxy-3-phenyl-2-propenamides as Novel Inhibitors of Human Histone
Deacetylase with in Vivo Antitumor Activity: Discovery of
(2E)-N-Hydroxy-3-[4-[[(2-hydroxyethyl)[2-(1H-indol-3-yl)ethyl]amino]methyl]phenyl]-2-propenamide
(NVP-LAQ824)
