$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of 3(R)-1,3-dibenzyl-4-propionylpiperazin-2-one (6b). To a 0
°C stirring suspension of D-phenylalanine methyl ester hydrochloride (153
mg, 0.709 mmol, 1.0 equiv.), 4Å powdered molecular sieves (250 mg),
acetic acid (120 μL, 2.13 mmol, 3.0 equiv.) and sodium
triacetoxyborohydride (225 mg, 1.06 mmol, 1.5 equiv.) in 5 mL
acetonitrile was added dropwise over 5 minutes a 2.5 mL acetonitrile
solution of aldehyde 4b (160 mg, 0.780 mmol, 1.1 equiv.). After stirring
for 90 minutes, the ice bath was removed and the reaction was warmed to
ambient temperature and stirred for 18 hours. The reaction was heated to
reflux for 8 days, cooled and poured into aqueous saturated NaHCO3, which
was extracted three times with dichloromethane. The combined organic
extracts were dried with Na2SO4, filtered and concentrated in vacuo.
Purification by flash chromatography (5% methanol in
dichloromethane)provided piperazinone 6b as clear oil (181 mg, 76%
yield). Chiral HPLC analysis (Chiralcel OD column 250 X 4.6 mm; 220 nm;
flow = 1.0 mL/minute of A/B:85/15 (A=hexanes, B=ethanol); 30 minute run.
64.8% enantiomeric excess. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) (Rotamer A:B; 1.7:1)
Rotamer A: δ 7.37-7.21 (m, 8H), 7.21-7.16 (m, 2H), 4.95 (d, J = 14.6 Hz,
1H), 4.67 (br d, J = 10.5 Hz, 1H), 4.28 (d, J = 14.6 Hz, 1H), 3.50 (dd, J
= 12.9, 4.9 Hz, 1H), 3.40-3.27 (m, 1H), 3.24-3.10 (m, 1H), 3.06 (dd, J =
12.2, 4.1 Hz, 1H), 2.89 (td, J = 12.8, 4.0 Hz, 1H), 2.28 (q, J = 7.4 Hz,
2H), 1.40 (m, 1H), 0.82 (t, J = 7.5 Hz, 3H): Rotamer B: δ 7.37-7.21 (m,
8H), 7.21-7.16 (m, 2H), 4.89 (d, J = 14.6 Hz, 1H), 4.56 (br d, J = 11.0
Hz, 1H), 4.33 (d, J = 14.6 Hz, 1H), 3.44 (br d, J = 13.7 Hz, 1H),
3.40-3.27 (m, 1H), 3.24-3.10 (m, 1H), 2.77 (br d, J = 12.0 Hz, 1H), 2.57
(td, J = 10.6, 3.3 Hz, 1H), 2.36 (q, J = 7.4 Hz, 2H), 1.92 (m, 1H), 1.13
(t, J = 7.5 Hz, 3H). HRMS (ES) exact mass calculated for C21H25N2O2
(M+H+): 337.1911; found 337.1910. Retention time for 6b = 10.3 minutes
(Area % = 68.96), enantiomer retention time = 16.9 minutes (Area % =
14.76);
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM mol. sieves used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Preparation of Substituted Piperazinones via Tandem Reductive
Amination-(N,N'-Acyl Transfer)-Cyclization
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Beshore, Douglas C.; Dinsmore, Christopher J.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2002), 4(7), 1201-1204

