$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of 1-Benzyl
5,5-dimethyl-2,3-dihydro-1H-pyrrolo[1,2a]imidazol-6(5H)-one (10). To a 0
°C stirring suspension of α-amino-iso-butyric acid methyl ester
hydrochloride (125 mg, 0.814 mmol, 1.0 equiv.), 4Å powdered molecular
sieves (250 mg), acetic acid (140 μL, 2.44 mmol, 3.0 equiv.) and sodium
triacetoxyborohydride (259 mg, 1.22 mmol, 1.5 equiv.) in 5 mL
acetonitrile was added dropwise over 5 minutes a 2.5 mL acetonitrile
solution of aldehyde 4a (171 mg, 0.90 mmol, 1.1 equiv.). After stirring
for 90 minutes, the ice bath was removed and the reaction was warmed to
ambient temperature and stirred for 18 hours. The pressure tube was
sealed and heated to 120 °C for 72 hours, cooled and poured into aqueous
saturated NaHCO3, which was extracted three times with dichloromethane.
The combined organic extracts were dried (Na2SO4), filtered and
concentrated in vacuo. Purification by flash chromatography (5% methanol
in dichloromethane) provided bicycle 10 as clear oil (147 mg, 75% yield).
1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.39- 7.28 (m, 3H), 7.27-7.24 (m, 2H), 4.54 (s,
1H), 4.39 (s, 2H), 3.57 (t, J = 7.7 Hz, 2H), 3.40 (t, J = 7.7 Hz, 2H).
HRMS (ES) exact mass calculated for C15H19N2O (M+H+): 243.1493; found
243.1490.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM mol. sieves used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Preparation of Substituted Piperazinones via Tandem Reductive
Amination-(N,N'-Acyl Transfer)-Cyclization
