$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the synthesis of
Aryl-Prop-2-ynyl-amine or Alkyl-Prop-2-ynylamine (C): Propargylamine
(171μL; 2.5mmol, 1 equiv) and aldehyde (3mmol; 1.2 equiv) are mixed in
dichloromethane (3mL), and then sodium triacetoxyborohydride (848mg;
4mmol, 1.6 equiv) is added. The reaction media is stirred under a stream
of argon at room temperature for 4 hours. Dichloromethane (20mL) is added
and the organic layer is washed with NaHCO3 5 % (2x20mL), with brine
(1x20mL) then with HCl 1N (20mL). The aqueous layer is then basified with
NaOH 1N (30mL) and extracted with ethyl acetate (2x20mL). The organic
layer was washed with brine then dried over MgSO4 and reduced under
pressure to give the desired compound.
Furan-3-ylmethyl-methyl-prop-2-ynyl-amine (30) was prepared following the
general procedure C using Furan-3-carbaldehyde to afford 224 mg (75%) of
Furan-3-ylmethyl-methyl-prop-2-ynyl-amine as orange oil. LC-MS (EI(+)):
m/z 150 [M+H]+; RT = 1.53 min; 1H NMR (CD2Cl2): 7.36 (m, 1H), 7.32 (m,
1H), 6.36 (m, 1H), 3.38 (s, 2H), 3.25 (d, 2H, J=2.4 Hz), 2.24 (m, 4H);
13C NMR (CD2Cl2): 144.2, 142.5, 112.3, 50.9, 45.7, 42.4.
