$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(2):CAS_RN
$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Potassium (4-((Piperidin-1-yl)methyl)furan-2-yl)trifluoroborate. A test
tube containing activated 4 Å molecular sieves (400 mg) and potassium
(4-formylfuran-2-yl)trifluoroborate (192mg, 0.95 mmol) was evacuated
under vacuum (0.01 Torr) for 15min. DMF (1 mL), piperidine (212 mg, 2.49
mmol), and formic acid (69 mg, 1.5 mmol) were added with stirring, and
the solution was then heated under nitrogen for 5 h at 70 °C. Palladium
acetate (22 mg, 0.10 mmol, 10 mol %) and potassium formate (195 mg, 2.32
mmol) were then added, and stirring was continued for an additional 4 h.
Heat was removed, the reaction mixture was filtered, and the white solid
was rinsed with MeOH (3 x 5 mL). To thefiltrate was added an aqueous
solution of KHF2 (1 mL, 4.4 M) with stirring, which was continued for 1
h. The solution was then concentrated under vacuum. The resulting yellow
solid was extracted with 10% MeOH in acetone (3 x 5 mL). This was
concentrated and precipitated with Et2O (10 mL) to give the prduct.
Potassium (4-((Piperidin-1-yl)methyl)furan-2-yl)trifluoroborate as a
yellow solid, yield 190 mg, 74%. Mp: greater than 200 °C. IR: 2933, 1669
cm-1. 1H NMR (500 MHz, acetone-d6): δ 1.38-1.44 (m, 2H), 1.52-1.60 (m,
4H), 2.10-2.16 (m, 4H), 3.44 (s, 2H), 6.21 (s, 1H), 7.30 (s, 1H). 13C NMR
(125.8 MHz, acetone-d6): δ 23.7, 25.1, 53.1, 53.1, 113.1, 140.8. 19F NMR
(471 MHz, acetone-d6): δ -142.1. 11B NMR (128 MHz, acetone-d6): δ 0.662.
HRMS (ESI): m/z calcd for C10H14BF3NO (M - K) 232.1121, found 232.1129.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM molecular sieves used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Functionalization of Organotrifluoroborates: Reductive Amination
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Molander, Gary A.; Cooper, David J.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2008), 73(10), 3885-3891

