$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure B for the Reductive
Amination of Potassium(Formylaryl)trifluoroborates using Pyridine-Borane.
Potassium(3-((Pyrrolidin-1-yl)methyl)phenyl)trifluoroborate. To a test
tube containing potassium (3-formylphenyl)trifluoroborate (106 mg, 0.50
mmol) and KHF2 (156 mg, 2.00 mmol) in MeOH (2 mL) was added pyrrolidine
(53 mg, 0.75 mmol). This was stirred for 2 h at room temperature.
Pyridine-borane (46 mg, 0.5 mmol) was then added, and stirring was
continued for 16 h. The solvent was then removed, and the resulting white
solid was rinsed with Et2O (2 x 5 mL). The resulting solid was then
extracted with 10% MeOH/acetone (3 x 5 mL), after which the combined
extracts were concentrated and precipitated with Et2O (10 mL) to give
product. Potassium
3-((4-(tert-Butoxycarbonyl)-piperazin-3-yl)methyl)phenyltrifluoroborate
as a yellow crystalline solid, yield 139 mg, 73%. Mp: greater than 200
°C.; IR (KBr) = 2975 cm-1; 1H NMR (500 MHz, acetone-d6): δ 1.42 (s, 9H),
2.35 (s, 4H), 3.33 - 3.41 (m, 4H), 3.49 (s, 2H), 7.03 - 7.09 (m, 2H),
7.37 - 7.40 (m, 1H), 7.45 (s, 1H); 13C NMR (125.8 MHz, acetone-d6): δ
27.7, 52.8, 63.5, 78.6, 126.3, 126.4, 130.6, 132.7, 135.2, 154.2, 205.5;
19F NMR (471 MHz, acetone-d6): δ -142.5; 11B NMR (128 MHz, acetone-d6): δ
4.06; HRMS (ESI): calcd for C16H23BF3N2O2 [M-K]- 343.1804, found343.1821.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Functionalization of Organotrifluoroborates: Reductive Amination
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Molander, Gary A.; Cooper, David J.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2008), 73(10), 3885-3891

