$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of
4-[(5-{[(2R)-4-(5-{[tert-butyl(diphenyl)silyl]oxy}-2-chlorobenzyl)-2-methyl-3-oxopiperazin-1-yl]carbonyl}-1H-imidazol-1-
yl)methyl]-2-fluorobenzonitrile (20). To a 0 °C stirring suspension of
D-alanine methyl ester hydrochloride (85 mg, 0.61 mmol, 1.0 equiv.), 4Å
powdered molecular sieves (200 mg), acetic acid (104 μL, 1.83 mmol, 3.0
equiv.) and sodium triacetoxyborohydride (194 mg, 0.913 mmol, 1.5 equiv.)
in 5 mL acetonitrile was added a 2.5 mL acetonitrile solution of aldehyde
19 (486 mg, 0.73 mmol, 1.2 equiv.) dropwise. After stirring for 90
minutes, the ice bath was removed and the reaction was warmed to ambient
temperature and stirred for 18 hours. The reaction was heated to reflux
for 3 hours, cooled and poured into aqueous saturated NaHCO3, which was
extracted three times with dichloromethane. The combined organic extracts
were dried (Na2SO4), filtered and concentrated in vacuo. Purification by
flash chromatography (0 to 4% methanol with 10% NH4OH in dichloromethane)
provided piperazinone 20 (317 mg, 72%). 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.70
(d, J = 6.8 Hz, 2H), 7.66 (s, 1H), 7.64 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 2H), 7.58 (dd, J
= 7.8, 6.8 Hz, 1H), 7.46-7.40 (m, 1H), 7.39 (d, J = 7.6 Hz, 2H), 7.36 (t,
J = 5.4 Hz, 1H), 7.34 (t, J = 7.1 Hz, 2H), 7.25 (s, 1H), 7.17 (d, J = 8.8
Hz, 1H), 6.98 (s, 1H), 6.97 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 1H), 6.79 (dd, J = 8.7, 2.8
Hz, 1H), 6.34 (br s, 1H), 5.45 (d, J = 15.6 Hz, 1H), 5.38 (d, J = 15.9
Hz, 1H), 5.30 (s, 2H), 4.87 (d, J = 15.6 Hz, 1H), 4.65 (br s, 1H), 4.00
(br t, J = 5.1 Hz, 2H), 2.58 (br s, 1H), 1.12 (d, J = 7.3 Hz, 3H), 1.06
(s, 9H). HRMS (ES) exact mass calcd for C40H40ClFN5O3Si (M+H+): 720.2568;
found 720.2534.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM mol. sieves used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
