$DATUM 5-(Benzyloxymethyl)-7-{[(1,3-dihydroxypropan-2-yl)(methyl)amino]
methyl}-4-methoxy-5H-pyrrolo[3,2-d]pyrimidine (46). Acetyl chloride (8.91
μL, 0.125 mmol) was added to MeOH (5 mL) with stirring and then 45 (155
mg, 0.42 mmol), paraformaldehyde (62 mg, 2.08 mmol), and sodium
cyanoborohydride (39 mg, 0.62 mmol) were added. After 16 h, the reaction
mixture was concentrated in vacuo and the residue purified by
chromatography (CHCl3/MeOH/ 28% aq NH4OH = 95:5:0.5) to afford 46 (115
mg, 72%) as a colorless gum. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CD3OD): δ 8.40 (s, 1H),
7.61 (s, 1H), 7.26-7.18 (m, 5H), 5.74 (s, 2H), 4.50 (s, 2H), 4.10 (s,
3H), 3.95 (s, 2H), 3.77 (dd, J =11.4, 7.3 Hz, 2H), 3.65 (dd, J = 11.4,
5.6 Hz, 2H), 2.93 (m, 1H), 2.37 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (125.7 MHz, CD3OD,
center line at δ 49.0): δ 157.9, 151.1, 150.6, 138.8, 134.6, 129.3,
128.7, 128.6, 117.2, 115.8, 78.5, 71.5, 66.3, 60.3, 60.3, 54.3, 48.1,
38.2. ESI-HRMS for C20H20N4O4 [MH+] calcd, 387.2032; found, 387.2034.
