$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (1-Isopropyl-piperidin-4-yl)-methanol (7) To a solution of
4-piperidinemethanol (10 g, 86.8 mmol) and acetone (50 g, 868 mmol) in
CH2Cl2 was added sodium triacetoxyborohydride (27.6 g, 130 mmol). After
stirring for 12 h, 10% NaOH solution (600 mL) was added and allowed to
stir for 4 h. After separation of the organic and aqueous portions, the
aqueous portion was extracted with ethyl acetate twice. The combined
organics were then washed with brine, dried over Na2SO4 and concentrated.
The viscous oil was distilled (100°C, 1 mm Hg) to provide the desired
product (9.7 g, 71%). (1-Isopropyl-piperidin-4-yl)-methanol (7), Yield
9.7 g, 71% 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 4.26 (br s, 1H), 3.34 (d, J = 6.6
Hz, 2H), 2.81 (dm, J = 11.4 Hz, 2H), 2.66-2.58 (m, 1H), 2.04 (dt, J =
2.5, 12.1 Hz, 2H), 1.69 (d, J = 12.4 Hz, 2H), 1.45-1.32 (m, 1H),
1.23-1.10 (m, 2H), 0.97 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 6H). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δ
= 67.4, 54.9, 48.9, 39.1, 29.4, 18.6. HRMS (EI): m/z calcd for C9H20NO
[M+H]+, 158.1545; found, 158.1542
