$DATUM Pyridine carboxaldehyde (0.107 g, 1 mmol) was dissolved in 1,2-DCE (4 mL)
and to it was added (Trz)2NH (0.359, 1 mmol), followed by brief
sonication. Na[BH(OAc)3] (95%, 0.335 g, 1.5 mmol) was poured in and the
reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature overnight. The yellow
reaction was quenched with NaHCO3/ NaOH and diluted with CH2Cl2, while
maintaining the aqueous pH 8-9. The product was extracted with
dichloromethane (3 × 20 mL), the combined organic layers were washed with
H2O, dried over anhydrous MgSO4, filtered and concentrated under vacuum,
then treated with 2.0 M ammonia in anhydrous methanol (2 mL, 4 mmol).
After 12 hours the volatiles were removed under reduced pressure.Compound
15, as pale orange oil (0.082, 71%). ESI-MS: m/z 387.2 (M+H+), 409.2
(M+Na+). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.48 (d, J = 4.6 Hz, 1H), 7.75 (s,
2H), 7.66 (td, J = 7.7, 1.2 Hz,1H), 7.54 (dm, J = 7.7 Hz, 1H), 7.19 -
7.13 (m, 1H), 4.49 (t, J = 6.6 Hz, 4H), 3.77 (s, 2H), 3.74 (s, 4H), 3.71
(br, 1H), 3.57 (t, J = 5.8 Hz, 4H), 2.14 - 2.06 (m, 4H). 13C NMR (101
MHz, CDCl3) δ 158.80, 148.99, 143.98, 137.03, 124.48, 123.94, 122.48,
63.83, 59.36, 58.35, 47.94, 32.61.
