$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the decarboxylative
cyclization of 9 to give the target compounds 1c, 1e, 1h, 1j, 1q. A
selected compound 9 and p-toluenesulfonic acid monohydrate were mixed in
a 1 to 2 molar ratio in toluene (10 mL per mmol of 9). With a Dean-Stark
trap, the reaction mixture was refluxed for 1 h. Solvent was removed
under vacuum, the residue basified with 1N NaOH, and then partitioned
with ethyl acetate. The organic phase was separated, washed with brine,
dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, and evaporated to give crude product, which
was, in most cases, pure by TLC. Analytical samples were obtained by
flash chromatography on silica gel (yield: 70 - 90%). 1h, yield 90% MS:
(APCI+) m/e [M+H] 353.29. 1H (CDCl3): δ 7.27 - 7.14 (m, 3H), 7.00 (td, J=
7.3, 1.2 Hz, 1H), 4.32 (tt, J= 12.6, 4.3 Hz, 1H), 3.50 (s, 2H), 3.32 -
2.98 (m, 2H), 2.54 - 1.06 (m, 23H). 13C{1H} (CDCl3): δ 175.1 (1C), 144.1
(1C), 127.7 (1C), 125.0 (1C), 124.7 (1C), 122.0 (1C), 110.8 (1C), 66.7
(1C), 50.7 (1C), 50.5 (1C), 50.4 (1C), 39.5 (1C), 37.0 (1C), 36.1 (1C),
32.8 (1C), 28.8 (1C), 28.6 (1C), 27.1 (1C), 25.9 (1C), 25.3 (1C), 24.6
(1C), 21.8 (1C), 20.6 (1C). Cald. (C23H32N2O) %: C, 78.36; H, 9.15; N,
7.95. Found %: C, 78.23; H, 9.18; N, 7.90.
