$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: The following is a typical experimental
procedure: a mixture of cyclohexanedione monoethylene ketal (1.6g, 10
mmol), methyl 4-aminobutyrate-HCl (2.38 g, 1S.S mmol), TEA (S g, SO mmol)
and NaBH(OAc)3 (3.0 g, 14 mmol) in DCE (30 mL) was stirred at rt for 45h
undo: nitrogen. The reaction was quenched with water and the product was
extracted with CH2Cl2 (3x80 mL). The CH2Cl2 extract was dried(MgSO4) and
the solvent was evaporated in vacuo to give a light brown oil (3.4 g).
The oil was dissolved in hexane with a trace of ether, the solution was
decanted from a dark oily residue, and the solvent was evaporated to
give. Table I, Entry 10, yield 70%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, in-situ generated reactant
