$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of 3(R)-4-acetyl-1,3-dibenzylpiperazin-2-one (6a). To a 0 °C
stirring suspension of D-phenylalanine methyl ester hydrochloride (100
mg, 0.464 mmol, 1.0 equiv.), 4Å powdered molecular sieves (200 mg),
acetic acid (83 μL, 1.4 mmol, 3.0 equiv.) and sodium
triacetoxyborohydride (147 mg, 0.693 mmol, 1.5 equiv.) in 5 mL
acetonitrile was added dropwise over 5 minutes a 2.5 mL acetonitrile
solution of aldehyde 4a (106 mg, 0.557 mmol, 1.1 equiv.). After stirring
for 90 minutes, the ice bath was removed and the reaction was warmed to
ambient temperature and stirred for 18 hours. The reaction was heated to
reflux for 7 hours, cooled and poured into aqueous saturated NaHCO3,
which was extracted three times with dichloromethane. The combined
organic extracts were dried (Na2SO4), filtered and concentrated in vacuo.
Purification by flash chromatography (0 to 50% ethyl acetate in
dichloromethane) provided piperazinone 6a as clear oil (103 mg, 69%
yield). Chiral HPLC analysis (Chiralcel AD column 250 X 4.6 mm; 220 nm;
flow = 1.0 mL/minute of A/B:4/6 (A = 0.1% diethylamine in hexanes, B =
ethanol); 20 minute run.95.1% enantiomeric excess. 1H NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3) (Rotamer A:B; 2.1:1) Rotamer A: δ 7.40-7.25 (m, 8H), 7.25-7.16 (m,
2H), 4.95 (d, J = 14.6 Hz, 1H), 4.66 (br dd, J = 13.8, 4.5 Hz, 1H), 4.50
(br dd, J = 9.5, 3.2 Hz, 1H), 4.29 (d, J = 14.6 Hz, 1H), 3.44-3.28 (m,
3H), 3.20 (dd, J = 13.5, 9.6 Hz, 1H), 3.07 (dd, J = 12.0, 4.1 Hz, 1H),
2.89 (ddd, J = 13.7, 13.4, 4.1 Hz, 1H) 1.46 (s, 3H): Rotamer B: δ
7.40-7.25 (m, 8H), 7.25-7.16 (m, 2H), 5.24 (br t, J = 4.8 Hz, 1H), 4.87
(d, J = 14.6 Hz, 1H), 4.34 (d, J = 14.6 Hz, 1H), 3.50 (dd, J = 13.4, 4.1
Hz, 1H), 3.44-3.28 (m, 3H), 3.26-3.15 (m, 1H), 2.76 (dt, J = 12.0, 3.0
Hz, 1H), 2.59 (td, J = 11.1, 3.5 Hz, 1H), 2.07 (s, 3H). HRMS (ES) exact
mass calculated for C20H23N2O2 (M+H+): 323.1754; found 323.1745.
Retention time for 6a = 17.4 minutes (Area % = 97.57), enantiomer
retention time = 6.5 minutes (Area % = 2.43);
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM mol. sieves used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Preparation of Substituted Piperazinones via Tandem Reductive
Amination-(N,N'-Acyl Transfer)-Cyclization
