$DATUM Diethyl (2S,3R)-2-Hydroxy-3-({[5-benzyloxymethyl-4-methoxy-
5H-pyrrolo[3,2-d]pyrimidin-7-yl]methyl}amino)butanedioate (54). Sodium
triacetoxyborohydride (0.545 g, 2.57 mmol) was added to a solution of
diethyl (2S,3R)-2-amino-3-hydroxysuccinate (50) 36 (0.53 g, 2.57 mmol,
prepared from diethyl-L-tartrate by known literature methods36,37) and
compound 44 8 (0.588 g, 1.98 mmol) in 1,2-dichloroethane (30 mL) and the
resulting reaction mixture stirred at room temperature for 4 h. The
mixture was then diluted with CH2Cl2 and washed with aqueous saturated
NaHCO3, dried, and concentrated in vacuo. The residue was purified by
chromatography (EtOAc/hexanes = 9:1→ EtOAc) to afford 54 (0.67 g, 69%) as
a pale-yellow gum. [α]D 21 -5.9 (c 0.54, EtOH). 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ, 8.55
(s, 1H), 7.34 (s, 1H), 7.33-7.23 (m, 5H), 5.70 (s, 2H), 4.62 (d, J = 3.4
Hz, 1H), 4.48 (s, 2H), 4.23-4.15 (m, 5H), 4.10 (s, 3H), 3.99 (d, J = 13.8
Hz, 1H), 3.85 (d, J = 3.3 Hz, 1H), 2.25 (br s, exchanged to D2O, 2H),
1.26 (t, J = 7.1 Hz, 3H), 1.25 (t, J = 7.1 Hz, 3H). 13C NMR (CDCl3,
center line at δ 77.0): δ 171.9, 171.1, 156.2, 150.0, 149.8, 136.9,
130.9, 128.4, 127.9, 127.6, 116.1, 77.0, 72.0, 70.2, 63.8, 61.4, 61.3,
53.5, 42.6, 14.1, 14.1. ESIHRMS for C24H31N4O7 [MH+] calcd, 487.2193;
found, 487.2174.
