$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM E-Salignone (1). Compound 9 (55.0 mg, 0.17 mmol) was dissolved in
dichloromethane (5 mL), and paraformaldehyde (423.7 mg, 14.11 mmol) was
added. The mixture was refluxed for 1 h, then sodium
triacetoxyhydroborate (64.0 mg, 0.30 mmol) was added, and the whole was
refluxed continuously for 2 h. Saturated NaHCO3 solution was added to
quench the reaction. The reaction mixture was extracted with
dichloromethane (15 mL), washed with water (45 mL), and dried. The
solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure to obtain the crude
product, which was purified by column chromatography over silica gel
(PE-EA 1:1-1:1 + 1% triethylamine) to give compound. Yield: (37.8 mg,
67.6%), colorless oil. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3, , ppm): 6.49 (1H, q, J =
7.2), 2.29 (6H, s), 1.84 (3H, d, J = 7.2), 1.01 (3H, s), 0.82 (3H, s).
13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3, , ppm): 206.6, 148.0, 128.9, 64.1, 54.2, 50.1,
45.6, 43.4, 41.7, 38.0, 37.4, 36.4, 34.2, 32.0, 31.0, 28.8, 24.7, 20.9,
17.7, 13.2, 12.3. ESI-MS m/z 344.6 [M + H]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Eschweiler-Clarke reaction, paraformaldehyde used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and Antimetastatic Effect of E-salignone
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
