$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Parallel Synthesis
of Aliphatic Sulfonamides. To a reaction vial containing an amine (0.7
mmol), an aldehyde (0.7 mmol), and TMSOAc (2.1 mmol) was added 0.25 mL of
a 2% solution of ZnCl2 in DMF. The vial was heated at 100 °C for 8 h and
allowed to cool to room temperature. Then NaBH(OAc)3 (1.4 mmol) was
added, and the mixture was kept at room temperature for 72 h with
occasional shaking. After subsequent sonication at 50-55 °C, the mixture
was treated with 1mL of 10% KOH solution followed by the addition of 7 mL
of water. The product was extracted with 3 mL of CHCl3, and the organic
phase was washed with water (2 × 7 mL) and evaporated. Compounds with
purity below 95% were subjected to further purification by flash
chromatography. N-(4-fluorobenzyl)-5-methylisoxazol-3-amine (Entry 1, in
Table 1) Enrty: 7; yield: 67%.
