$DATUM 2-(4-(dimethylamino)phenyl)-8-(1,4-dioxa-7,13-dithia-10-azacyclopentadecan-10-yl)methylfuro[3,2-h]quinoline
(FQ-crown): To a mixture of 15 (0.40 g, 1.26 mmol) and azacrown[N,S,O]s1
(0.30 g, 1.19 mmol) in 1,2-dichloroethane (20 mL) was added NaBH(OAc)3
(0.41 g, 1.93 mmol). The resulting solution was stirred at room
temperature overnight. The solution was acidified with 1N HCl to pH 4-5.
Then it was neutralized with 1 N NaOH to pH 7-8. Organic phase was
separated. Aqueous phase was extracted with DCM (2 x 20mL). Organic
phases were combined and dried over Na2SO4. The solvents were evaporated
to give crude oil, which was purified by chromatography (silica gel,
petroleum / 0-5% acetone) to generate yellow solid (0.42 g, 65%). mp:
66-68 ° C. 1H NMR (400MHz, CD3OD, ppm) δ 8.31 (1H, d, J = 8.2 Hz), 7.92
(2H, d, J = 8.0 Hz), 7.73 (2H, m), 7.65 (1H, d, J = 8.4 Hz), 7.08 (1H,
s), 6.86 (2H, d, J = 8.2 Hz), 4.05 (2H, s), 3.76 (4H, t, J = 5.5 Hz),
3.65 (4H, s), 3.03 (6H, s), 2.89 (8H, s), 2.72 (4H, t, J = 5.4Hz). 13C
NMR (100MHz, CDCl3, ppm): δ 160.88, 158.31, 150.77, 148.57, 137.01,
136.13, 129.76, 126.75, 125.07, 122.96, 119.74, 119.31, 11.66, 112.19,
99.47, 73.52, 71.04, 62.49, 54.73, 40.48, 31.61, 30.51. Mass (MALDI-TOF):
m/z 552.3 (M+H+). HRMS (ESI): calcd for C30H38N3O3S2 (M+H+)+ 552.23491,
found 552.23383. ΔM = 2.0 ppm.
