$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM O-Benzyl-N-methyl-5-hydroxy-1-aminoindan Hydrochloride. A mixture of
indanone compound (3.45 g, 14.5 mmol), 8 M ethanolic methylamine (15 mL,
120 mmol), MeNH2 hydrochloride (3.6 g, 53 mmol), NaCNBH3 (1.47 g, 23.4
mmol), dry THF (375 mL), and MeOH (125 mL) was stirred and heated at
reflux under N2 for 8 h. The mixture was cooled to 5 °C and acidified to
pH 1 with concentrated HCl. Evaporation at 45 °C gave a tan solid that
was treated with CH2Cl2 (250 mL) and water (250 mL). The resulting
mixture was separated, and the aqueous layer was re-extracted with CH2Cl2
(10 x 60 mL). The combined organic layer was washed with water (150 mL)
and brine (150 mL) and dried (Na2SO4). Evaporation of solvent at reduced
pressure gave a light tan solid that was purified by flash chromatography
(CH2Cl2/MeOH, 4:1) to give 3.0 g of a light yellow solid. The solid was
further purified by stirring it with hexane (50 mL) at 25 °C for 30 min
and filtering. The hexane washing was repeated one more time to give
O-Benzyl-N-methyl-5-hydroxy-1-aminoindan Hydrochloride, yield 2.70 g, 64%
as a yellowish solid. mp 174-176 °C. 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 7.6-7.57 (d, 1H, J
= 9.1 Hz), 7.31-7.2 (m, 5H), 6.8-6.78 (m, 2H), 4.91 (s, 2H), 4.48-4.44
(dd, 1H, J = 7.7, 3.2 Hz), 3.23-3.17 (m, 1H), 2.84-2.81 (m, 1H),
2.41-2.09 (m, 5H). MS (CI/NH3) m/z 254 (MH+, 20), 222 ([M - NHCH3]+,
100), 132 (C9H10N, 98).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Hydroxy-1-aminoindans and Derivatives: Preparation, Stability, and
Reactivity
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Herzig, Yaacov; Lerman, Lena; Goldenberg, Willy; Lerner, David; Gottlieb,
Hugo E.; Nudelman, Abraham
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2006), 71(11), 4130-4140

